This project uses **sbrain** (installed as a Claude Code plugin).

Stack profile: [stack-nestjs | none (growing — rules accumulate in .agent/memory/STACK.md)]

## Non-negotiables (details live in the kernel skills and docs/)

- Git is the source of truth; `.agent/` state files are caches reconciled at session start.
- Run `sbrain:session-start` before any work; `sbrain:session-end` to close.
- One task per branch off `develop`; never commit to `main`/`develop` (hook-enforced).
- Contract first: no code for a module before `docs/modules/[module]/CONTRACT.md` exists.
- No new dependency without human approval; deviations from rules require an ADR.
- Every non-WIP commit passes the fresh-context `code-reviewer` agent first.

## Where things live

- Rules: `docs/RULES.md` · Architecture + enabled concerns: `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md`
- Task ledger: `.agent/tasks/INDEX.md` (generated — never edit by hand)
- Traps: `docs/KNOWN_ISSUES/INDEX.md` · Decisions: `.agent/memory/DECISIONS.md`, `docs/ADR/`
